  <entry>
    <id>https://www.thunderbird.net/en-US/thunderbird/155.0/releasenotes/</id>
    <title type="html">Thunderbird 155.0</title>
    <author>
      <name>Thunderbird</name>
      <uri>https://www.thunderbird.net</uri>
    </author>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.thunderbird.net/en-US/thunderbird/155.0/releasenotes/"/>
    <updated>2026-09-01T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
    <published>2026-09-01T00:00:00+00:00</published>

    <content type="html"><![CDATA[
      

  
  

  
    

    
      
        
        

        
          <h3>What’s New</h3>
        

        
        
          <ul>
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>S/MIME popup shows signature, digest, encryption algorithms and key sizes</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Default address book for manually added contacts configurable with <code>mail.addr_book.add_item_default_uri</code></p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Enterprise policy <code>DisableQRExport</code> can disable QR export</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>OAuth add-ons can override built-in settings for selected domains and hostnames</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Manual account config streamlined with Exchange, Graph, and custom OAuth support</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Custom OAuth support for IMAP and SMTP servers</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>PKCE and external browser fields added to custom OAuth settings</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Enterprise policy <code>DisableExperimentalFeatures</code> for disabling experimental features</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        
          </ul>
        

        
          <h3>Fixed</h3>
        

        
        
          <ul>
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Unread count dock badge disappeared on macOS restart when no mail window opened</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>IMAP tags did not sync automatically across clients</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Embedded SVG images appeared broken when Display Attachments Inline was disabled</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Holding arrow keys failed to smoothly navigate the folder pane</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Mark and Tag menu bar items were disabled in search results</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Quick Filter ignored address book display names shown in message lists and headers</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Attachment filters could disappear or return no results in global search</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Body search failed for quoted-printable messages ending on a soft line break</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Failed encrypted send did not preserve draft</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Failed account setup left an incoming server that blocked account recreation</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Removing an account did not remove its OAuth token from the password manager</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Account Hub prompted for calendar credentials immediately after successful login</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Filters could copy empty messages to Local Folders during startup mail download</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Closing message filters wrongly warned completed newsgroup filters were running</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Autoscroll icon was missing directional arrows in scrollable messages</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Apple Mail text attachments may not appear in MIME messages</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Forwarded messages could display incorrect encoding</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Thunderbird could crash due to improper database memory handling</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Thunderbird could crash on shutdown while waiting for OAuth2 password entry</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Thunderbird could crash while loading mail folders</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Custom OAuth could not be disabled</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Legacy IMAP tag changes were not sent to the server and reverted after refresh</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Deleting an Exchange account retained the outgoing server settings</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>CalDAV calendars with offline support could stop fully synchronizing events</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Offline cached ICS calendar changes were silently lost after reconnecting</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Thunderbird upgrade disabled composition toolbar</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Thunderbird upgrade disabled Settings menu for versions before macOS 13</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

        <li>
          <p>Windows jump list menu no longer functioned correctly</p>
          
        </li>
      
    
      
        
        

        

        
        

        
        

